Balance beginOffscreenFrame() on every fallback path.

After rhi->beginOffscreenFrame() SUCCEEDS, two failure fallbacks
(createTextures failing — which is exactly the poisoned-buffer path fixed
by 0001 — and updateTextures failing) return into convertCPU() WITHOUT
rhi->endOffscreenFrame(). The shared converter RHI is left permanently
recording (isRecordingFrame() stuck true): every later toImage() then fails
beginOffscreenFrame and silently degrades to CPU conversion, and the open
frame's resources are never reclaimed. Consume the pending resource-update
batch and end the frame before falling back.

--- a/src/multimedia/video/qvideoframeconverter.cpp
+++ b/src/multimedia/video/qvideoframeconverter.cpp
@@ (anchors; apply with tools/build-patched-qt/apply-0003.py)
     auto videoFrameTextures = QVideoTextureHelper::createTextures(frameTmp, *rhi, *rub, texturesTmp);
     if (!videoFrameTextures) {
         qCDebug(qLcVideoFrameConverter) << "Failed obtain textures. Using CPU conversion.";
+        cb->resourceUpdate(rub);
+        rhi->endOffscreenFrame();
         return convertCPU(frame, transformation);
     }
 
     if (!updateTextures(rhi, uniformBuffer, textureSampler, shaderResourceBindings,
                         graphicsPipeline, renderPass, frameTmp, videoFrameTextures)) {
         qCDebug(qLcVideoFrameConverter) << "Failed to update textures. Using CPU conversion.";
+        cb->resourceUpdate(rub);
+        rhi->endOffscreenFrame();
         return convertCPU(frame, transformation);
     }
